<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
    Cheep Cheep Family: field additions for Yaz0moto.

    WHAT THIS ADDS, AND WHY IT IS DEFENSIBLE
    ========================================
    The retail game binds every Pukupuku-family actor to the shared movement
    system in its onCreate:

        movementHandler.link(position,
                             movementHandler.getMaskForMovementType(settings2 & 0xFF),
                             movementId);

    Two things follow, and both are checkable against the stock editor's own data:

      * settings2 & 0xFF is the low byte of settings2. Yaz0moto stores settings2
        across nybbles 13-20 with nybble 20 holding bits 0-3, so that low byte is
        exactly nybbles 19-20.
      * movementId is Actor+0x1C, stored at nybbles 21-22.

    The base game already documents nybble 19-20 as "Movement Type" and 21-22 as
    "Movement ID" on 143 other sprites, so this is the engine's existing
    convention, not something invented here.

    Yet none of the eighteen Cheep-family sprites exposes those two nybbles
    (except the two grouped variants, which use 21-22 for their Group ID). That
    is the gap this patch closes: you can attach a Cheep Cheep to a movement
    controller without hand-editing raw nybbles.

    WHAT THIS DELIBERATELY DOES NOT DO
    ==================================
    * It does not touch `notes`. The merge behaviour for that attribute is not
      documented and could replace the base game's text, which would be a
      regression.
    * It does not rename any sprite.
    * It does not write to a nybble the base game already uses. Each sprite below
      was checked against the extracted "occupied nybble" set; sprites 615 and
      723 are given only 19-20 because 21-22 is their Group ID.
    * It does not claim the UNUSED sprites are usable. They are left as they are.

    CONFIDENCE
    ==========
    The movement binding comes from our decompilation of the Cheep Cheep
    constructor path and is cross-checked against the editor's own convention on
    143 sprites. It is not confirmed by loading a level in-game. If movement
    controllers turn out not to affect a given variant, that variant's two fields
    are inert rather than harmful.
-->
<sprites>

    <!-- ===== swimming variants ===== -->

    <!-- profile 530 -->
    <sprite id="101" name="Cheep Cheep">
        <value nybble="19-20" title="Movement Type" category="movement"
               comment="Shared movement system. 0 leaves the fish swimming on its own." />
        <value nybble="21-22" title="Movement ID" id_type="movement" category="movement"
               comment="Attach to a movement controller, rotation controller or path." />
    </sprite>

